  "source_text": {
    "prototype_id": "R03",
    "action": "Fertigate leek with calcium nitrate (nitrate N) 5 kg/στρ via drip = ~0.8 kg N/στρ. Do NOT top-dress urea on the surface. Do NOT give N to spinach (PL01, PL08), rocket (PL04, PL13) or other lots < 21 days from harvest.",
    "window": "Mon 23 - Wed 25 Nov (after the front, when drip restarts)",
    "why_rule": "N form must suit soil: on pH >= 7.5 with free lime, surface urea/ammonium loses NH3 unless incorporated by >= 10 mm rain or irrigation → use nitrate via fertigation. Not before heavy rain (leaching). Leafy greens: last N >= 21 days before harvest – winter low light raises leaf nitrate; EU sets maximum nitrate levels for spinach and rocket (Reg. (EU) 2023/915).",
    "severity": null
  },
  "notes": "QA P2-18 lesson: fertigating leek through the spinach drip sector feeds N to a harvesting spinach lot. Severity not given in RULES; High chosen because it is a block."
